<http://purl.org/cerif/frapo/supplies> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <http://purl.org/cerif/frapo/> .
<http://purl.org/cerif/frapo/isAwardedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The relation between something awarded and the agent making the award, for example linking a grant to a funding agency, a degree to a university, or a prize to the awarding organization."@en .
<http://purl.org/cerif/frapo/Account> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A mechanism for administering money, typically owned by an agent and dedicated to a particular purpose, for example the equipment account of a university department, to be used only for the purchase or maintenance of items of equipment. "@en .
<http://purl.org/cerif/frapo/DocumentRepository> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A facility in which digital documents are deposited for long-term preservation and (optional) publication."@en .
<http://purl.org/cerif/frapo/RegistrationAuthority> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An agent with responsibility for registering and maintaining international standards, internet domain names, patents, controlled vocabularies and other similar entities required for reliable international cooperatative activities. For example, the International DOI Foundation (IDF) is the Registration Authority for DOIs."@en .
<http://purl.org/cerif/frapo/isEnabledBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is enabled by"@en .
